# Auth API requests for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client).
# Start the API first: npm run dev -w server
# Then click "Send Request" above any request.

@api = http://localhost:4000/api
@email = test.student@mcmaster.ca
@password = longenough1

### Health check
GET {{api}}/health

### 1. Sign up -> 201. The verify link is printed in the server terminal ([email] Verify ...)
POST {{api}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}", "displayName": "Test Student" }

### 2. Log in before verifying -> 403 EMAIL_NOT_VERIFIED
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 3. Verify: paste the token from the link in the server terminal after token=
GET {{api}}/auth/verify-email?token_here

### 4. Log in -> 200 with a token
# @name login
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 5. Who am I -> 200 (uses the token from request 4 automatically)
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.token}}

### Seed user login (password123) -> 200
# @name seedLogin
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "seed.alex.chen@mcmaster.ca", "password": "password123" }

### Who am I as the seed user -> 200
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{seedLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### ---------- Things that should fail ----------

### Non-school email -> 400
POST {{api}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "someone@gmail.com", "password": "{{password}}", "displayName": "Nope" }

### Short password -> 400
POST {{api}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "short.pw@mcmaster.ca", "password": "short", "displayName": "Nope" }

### Same email twice -> 409 (run after request 1)
POST {{api}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}", "displayName": "Duplicate" }

### Wrong password -> 401
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "wrongpassword" }

### No token -> 401
GET {{api}}/auth/me

### Bad token -> 401
GET {{api}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-token

### Resend verification (same answer whether or not the account exists) -> 200
POST {{api}}/auth/resend-verification
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}" }
